{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KdvSNq6zuEh63zwLUN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft this, a few questions. Your answers will change what the letter says, and the hiring manager will likely be wondering about the same things:\n\n1. **Who is it going to?** What's the practice called, and do you have the name of the person hiring? In a small town, do you know anyone there, or is the practice a patient of the clinic you worked at?\n2. **Dentrix:** Have you started learning it, for example through a tutorial, a course or the free Dentrix training videos? Would you be willing to before you start? Have you used any other software since 2014 that shows you pick up new systems quickly?\n3. **Supervision:** At the clinic, did the 14 staff report to you directly? Did you hire, train, schedule or review them? The posting says the manager supervises 9 people, so this matters.\n4. **The drop in unpaid invoices:** What did you change to get them from $38,000 to $9,000? For example, payment plans, calling clients, or billing at checkout. One concrete step will be more convincing than the number alone.\n5. **References:** Can you still reach anyone from the clinic, such as a vet or the owner, who would vouch for you?\n6. **Anything they'll learn anyway:** Is there something a reference check or a small-town conversation would turn up? For example, why you left the clinic, whether it closed or was sold, or when you could start.\n\nIf you don't know the answer to any of these, just tell me. I'll write the letter without that detail instead of guessing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":9527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"inpu